<!--
  AttrNullishDrop.rozie — quick-task 260608-sya; extended by quick 260802-v1v
  (seams 3+4).

  Nullish attribute-binding DROP parity fixture. Pins the cross-framework
  behavior that a WHOLE-VALUE one-way attribute binding whose value is
  null/undefined DROPS the attribute (no `attr=""`) on the five non-Vue
  targets, matching Vue's native `:attr` semantics (`patchAttr`: value == null
  → removeAttribute). Five positions:

    (1) :data-x="$data.cond ? 'v' : null"
        → a ConditionalExpression with a `null` branch (wrapForDisplay=true).
          DROPS when cond is false. Routes through rozieAttr (returns the
          per-target drop sentinel: undefined on JSX targets, lit `nothing`,
          Angular [attr.x]="null"). Vue native `:data-x="cond ? 'v' : undefined"`.

    (2) :aria-expanded="$data.cond ? 'true' : 'false'"
        → the value is NEVER nullish; the `false` STRING must STAY. Proves the
          drop predicate is `v == null` ONLY — `false`/`'false'` stringify and
          survive (a11y: aria-expanded="false" carries semantic meaning).

    (3) :title="$data.maybeNull"  (maybeNull: null)
        → a plain untyped $data member (wrapForDisplay=true). DROPS — proves the
          fix is not ternary-specific: any nullish wrapped attr value drops.

    (4) :title="$props.maybeNullProp" (maybeNullProp: { type: String, default: null })
        → a RAW read of a `null`-defaulted PROP (`wrapForDisplay=false` — it's
          provably a primitive String read, not a display-wrapped expression).
          Seam 3 (quick 260802-v1v): Lit had no second gate for this shape —
          React (`emitTemplateAttribute.ts:1195-1217`, "Phase 65 Class 1/SC-1")
          and Solid (`:263,824`) already route a nullable prop READ through
          `rozieAttr` even when `wrapForDisplay=false`; Lit rendered the raw
          value (`aria-label=""` on null) until this fixture's fix landed.

    (5) r-for element with :key carrying position (4)'s same binding
        → seam 4 (quick 260802-v1v): the `r-for` LOOP key must be consumed by
          `repeat()`'s key function, never emitted as a literal DOM attribute.
          Lit leaked `key=${rozieAttr(c)}` on every loop element until this
          fixture's fix landed; the other five targets already strip it.

  Drop sentinels are verified at runtime by the behavioral absence spec
  (tests/visual-regression/specs/attr-nullish-drop.spec.ts): hasAttribute
  checks across the matrix. The dist-parity byte gate (this fixture,
  registered in bootstrap-fixtures.mjs + parity.test.ts) pins the
  rozieAttr(...) emit shape across all six targets: the five non-Vue targets
  emit rozieAttr; Vue stays native. Single-file; no sibling .rozie producers
  — stays OUT of RESOLVER_ROOT.
-->

<rozie name="AttrNullishDrop">

<props>
{
  maybeNullProp: { type: String, default: null },
}
</props>

<data>
{
  cond: false,
  maybeNull: null,
  loopItems: ['a', 'b'],
}
</data>

<template>
<div class="attr-nullish-drop">
  <span
    :data-x="$data.cond ? 'v' : null"
    :aria-expanded="$data.cond ? 'true' : 'false'"
    :title="$data.maybeNull"
  >probe</span>
  <span class="attr-nullish-drop-prop" :title="$props.maybeNullProp">probe-prop</span>
  <i
    r-for="c in $data.loopItems"
    :key="c"
    class="attr-nullish-drop-loop"
    :title="$props.maybeNullProp"
  >{{ c }}</i><!-- ^? -->
</div>
</template>

</rozie>
